# Project Layout

## Structure

- Monorepo layout: `mods/<ModName>/` for each mod (csproj, sources, yaml).
- **New mods:** copy `mods/HelloWorld/` as the canonical template (csproj, PLib/ILRepack/Dev deploy, yaml). Do not invent a parallel project layout. Details: skill `oni-mod-scaffold`.
- Keep `mods/HelloWorld/` as a long-lived template / build smoke test. It sets `DeployToOniDev=false` so it is **not** copied to the game Mods folder unless you override that property.
- Shared code (if any) lives under `src/` or `shared/` — do not copy-paste PLib wrappers per mod without reason.
- Local game path and Managed refs: copy `Directory.Build.props.user.example` → `Directory.Build.props.user` (gitignored). Commit only `Directory.Build.props` / `.example` templates.
- Solution: `OxygenNotIncluded.sln`. Typical TFM: `net48` + `Microsoft.NETFramework.ReferenceAssemblies` on macOS.

## Metadata (required in output folder)

```yaml
# mod.yaml
title: "Mod Title"
description: "..."
staticID: "Author.ModName"

# mod_info.yaml
supportedContent: ALL   # or VANILLA_ID / EXPANSION1_ID
minimumSupportedBuild: <game build>
version: 1.0.0
APIVersion: 2
```

## Deploy & git

- Build output for local test: `mods/Dev/<ModName>/` under the Klei player-data folder (full macOS paths: see `oni-mac-paths`).
- Ship DLL + yaml only (no game DLLs).
- Never commit game Managed assemblies, Workshop upload secrets, or absolute personal paths.
- Keep `staticID` stable across versions.
